% ADJ52 counterfactual-panel demo rulebook (illustrative, not clinical
% advice). A deliberately tiny rulebook with ONE decision-relevant
% uncertainty — a not-yet-performed biopsy — so the runner's
% value-of-information panel has something to surface.

% Prior: base rate of malignancy in this presentation.
prior 0.30 for diagnosis(malignancy)
  source "ADJ52 demo fixture — illustrative base rate"
  trust inferred

% A mediastinal mass on imaging strongly raises malignancy.
contributes 4.0 from imaging(mediastinal_mass) to diagnosis(malignancy)
  source "ADJ52 demo fixture — imaging likelihood ratio"
  trust inferred

% No improvement on broad-spectrum antibiotics argues against infection,
% i.e. raises malignancy.
contributes 2.5 from response(no_improvement_on_antibiotics) to diagnosis(malignancy)
  source "ADJ52 demo fixture — treatment-response likelihood ratio"
  trust inferred

% The biopsy is the decision-relevant uncertainty: it has not been
% performed yet. Each possible result carries its own likelihood ratio.
% A malignant-cell result is near-dispositive; a benign result nearly
% rules malignancy out. The `uncertain { … }` marker below tells the
% engine the domain is unresolved so it emits a VOI report.
contributes 50.0 from biopsy(malignant_cells) to diagnosis(malignancy)
  source "ADJ52 demo fixture — biopsy malignant is near-dispositive"
  trust inferred
contributes 0.02 from biopsy(benign) to diagnosis(malignancy)
  source "ADJ52 demo fixture — biopsy benign nearly rules out"
  trust inferred

% Mark the biopsy as an open uncertainty over its candidate results.
uncertain { biopsy(malignant_cells), biopsy(benign) } for diagnosis(malignancy)
  source "ADJ52 demo fixture — biopsy not yet performed"
